# Audio Reference Studio

Specs live in `docs/01_TECHNICAL_MVP_SPEC.md`, `docs/03_CURSOR_AGENT_FIRST_SESSION.md`, and `docs/04_TECHNICAL_CHART_REQUIREMENTS.md`. Follow them; do not copy them into code comments.

## Architecture

React/TypeScript frontend, Python 3.12/FastAPI backend, SQLite plus local files. Analysis that exists later is deterministic. Optional AI interpretation stays off by default.

## Local-first

Bind `127.0.0.1`. No cloud, auth, telemetry, payments, or paid API calls.

## Gates

Stop at the current milestone. Do not start the next one without human approval.

## Evidence

Use `measured`, `estimated`, `textual`, `interpretive`, or `unknown`. Never invent sung timestamps or audible-defect verdicts.

## Delegation

Agree the shared contract first. Frontend owns `frontend/**`. Backend owns `backend/**`. Neither edits the other's tree or `references/legacy-audit/`.

## Keep approved decisions

24-bit masters stay byte-identical; playback is a separate cached 16-bit derivative. Analyze stays unimplemented until a real worker exists, and it must not fake a completed job.

```python
# ❌ BAD — claims work that did not run
analysis_status = "completed"

# ✅ GOOD
analysis_status = "not_run"
```
